<%- include("./partials/header.ejs") %>
<article class="about-page">
    <section class="about-intro">
        <h1>Dear me,</h1>

        <p>It has been so long since I have talked to you.</p>
        <p>So here I am, with all the good, the bad and everything in between. Everything I was, everything I am, and everything I will be.</p>
        <p>I hope you'll be kind. I hope you'll listen. And I hope you'll walk alongside me through all of it.</p>
        <p>After all, who else could I ask to walk this path with me?</p>
    </section>

    <img class="divider" src="/images/assets/divider.svg" alt="">
    

    <section class="about-guide">
        <h2>A little guide to getting started</h2>

        <p>
            There is no right way to put your thoughts into words.
            But if you are wondering where to begin, here are a few
            little steps to help you along.
        </p>

        <ol>
            <li>
                <strong>Start wherever you are.</strong>
                You don't need a grand idea or a perfectly clear mind.
                Begin with whatever has been on your mind lately.
            </li>

            <li>
                <strong>Put it into words.</strong>
                Write about the good, the bad, the confusing, the
                unfinished, or even the things you cannot quite explain.
                You don't have to make it sound beautiful.
            </li>

            <li>
                <strong>Give your thoughts a home.</strong>
                Add a title that feels right, read through what you have
                written, and make any changes you feel like making.
            </li>

            <li>
                <strong>Let it be.</strong>
                When you're ready, save it for yourself or share it with others. It doesn't have to be perfect or have everything figured out. Sometimes, getting the words out is enough.
            </li>
        </ol>
    </section>

    <section class="about-restrict">
        <h2>A few things to remember</h2>

        <p>
            This little corner of the internet is a place for honest
            thoughts, but a few things are worth keeping in mind.
        </p>

        <ul>
            <li>Be kind to yourself. You are allowed to be a work in progress.</li>
            <li>Share only what you feel comfortable making public. Posts you share can be read by anyone, even without an account. Posts marked "Only me" stay in your journal.</li>
            <li>Respect other people's privacy when writing about them.</li>
            <li>Use a content warning if your writing touches something heavy.</li>
            <li>Let this be a space for reflection, not for hurting or humiliating others.</li>
            <li>You can edit or delete anything you've written, and you can delete your account whenever you like. Your thoughts today do not have to define you forever.</li>
            <li>If something you read worries or hurts you, you can report it.</li>
        </ul>

        <p>
            When you write, you can also add a sticker for how it feels, a time-of-day tag (a mood, not a clock), up to three topic tags, and a content warning, which tucks your words away until a reader chooses to open them. You can keep a post just for yourself or share it. You'll need an account to write, but anyone can read the posts that are shared. Your journal keeps everything you've written, and has a small space to note how you're feeling. Only you can see it.
        </p>
    </section>

    <img class="divider" src="/images/assets/divider.svg" alt="">

    <section class="about-privacy">
        <h2>Your privacy, honestly</h2>

        <p>Because people write vulnerable things here, I'd rather tell you exactly how this place works.</p>

        <ul>
            <li>Posts you choose to share can be read by anyone, with or without an account. Your pseudonym appears on them, along with the date, but never the time.</li>
            <li>Posts marked "Only me" can't be opened by anyone else. They don't appear on the home page, in search, or anywhere else. Your journal status is private in the same way.</li>
            <li>There's no email. The site keeps your pseudonym, your picture choice, your journal status, scrambled versions of your password and recovery code, and what you write.</li>
            <li>"Scrambled" means nobody can read your password or recovery code, including me.</li>
            <li>After you sign up, you'll see a recovery code once. It's the only way back in if you forget your password. If you lose both, the account can't be recovered.</li>
            <li>You can edit or delete your own posts, and switch a post between "Only me" and shared whenever you like. If a post was shared for a while, someone may already have read it.</li>
            <li>You can delete your account from your journal page. That removes your account and everything you've written, and it can't be undone.</li>
            <li>You can report a shared post. Reports are read only by me, and the writer is never told who sent one. I keep your pseudonym with a report so I can spot repeats, and it's removed from the report if you delete your account.</li>
            <li>The site uses one small cookie to keep you logged in, and nothing to track you. The fonts are served from this site, so nobody else is told that you visited.</li>
        </ul>

        <h3>What I can't promise</h3>

        <ul>
            <li>I run this site, so I can technically see everything stored in it, including posts marked "Only me". They're hidden from other people, but they aren't encrypted.</li>
            <li>The site is hosted on Railway, so your data sits on their servers too, and they may keep routine logs of requests, such as which pages were opened.</li>
            <li>Shared posts are not listed by search engines, but anyone with the link can read them.</li>
            <li>I'm one person, so reports may take a while to read. Since I hold no email addresses, I can't contact a writer, or tell them why I removed a post.</li>
            <li>The guidelines above are a request, not a guarantee. If something needs removing and you can't do it yourself, write to <a href="mailto:ankitadas8818@gmail.com">this email address</a> and I'll look at it.</li>
        </ul>
    </section>

    <aside class="about-note">
        <h2>If you're struggling</h2>

        <p>
            You don't have to figure everything out alone.
            Take a breath, reach out to someone you trust, or seek
            support when things feel heavy.
        </p>

        <p>
            In India, call
            <a href="tel:14416">14416</a> for free, 24/7 support
            through <a href="https://telemanas.mohfw.gov.in/"
            target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Tele-MANAS</a>.
            For other countries and support options, visit
            <a href="https://findahelpline.com/"
            target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Find A Helpline</a>.
        </p>
    </aside>

    <div class="about-cta">
        <p class="quote">Whenever you're ready, there's a little space here for you.</p>

        <% if (currentUser) { %>
            <a href="/compose" class="btn btn--solid">Write</a>
        <% } else { %>
            <a href="/register" class="btn btn--solid">Create an account to write</a>
            <p class="form-cross-link">Already have one? <a href="/login">Log in</a></p>
        <% } %>

    </div>
</article>


